/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
75 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (The objective of this assignment is to cluster words belonging to four semantic categories: Animals, Countries, Fruits, and Vegetables. The dataset consists of pre-trained GloVe word embeddings, where each word is represented by a 300-dimensional feature vector that captures semantic meaning and contextual similarity between words. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
76 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (The SOM model is based on the concept of Competitive Learning, where neurons compete to become the winning neuron, known as the Best Matching Unit \(BMU\). During training, the winning neuron and its neighboring neurons are updated in order to organize similar patterns into nearby regions within the map. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
77 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (In this assignment, different values of the parameter k, representing the number of neurons or clusters, were tested from 2 to 10 to analyze the clustering performance under different SOM configurations. The SOM algorithm was implemented entirely from scratch using Python and NumPy without relying on external SOM libraries. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
78 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (The clustering performance was evaluated using two external evaluation metrics: Purity and Rand Index. In addition, contingency tables and graphical visualizations were used to analyze and compare the clustering results for different values of k.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
