/P 60 0 R
/E (After the training process is completed, each input word is assigned to its corresponding Best Matching Unit \(BMU\). The BMU represents the neuron with the minimum Euclidean distance to the input vector. As a result, words with similar semantic representations are grouped into the same cluster. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (The cluster assignment process is performed by calculating the Euclidean distance between each input vector and all SOM neurons, then assigning the word to the neuron with the smallest distance. The predicted clusters are later used to build contingency tables and evaluate the clustering performance using Purity and Rand Index metrics. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (A Kohonen Self-Organizing Map \(SOM\) is an unsupervised neural network used for clustering high-dimensional data using Competitive Learning. In this model, each neuron contains a weight vector with the same dimensionality as the input data. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
